# HARNESS-106's copies are byte-for-byte oracles: the boundaries suite pins each
# by checksum and size, and its C-9 cases read them as real story sections. The
# root .gitattributes is not shipped by a refresh, so a consumer's own
# attributes and core.autocrlf would otherwise decide their line endings on
# checkout and turn an oracle into a different file. Nothing here is converted.
* -text
